WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.293
Step 1. On the encounter's overview, select New Referral in the quick actions.

1.2
00:00:05.293 --> 00:00:10.466
You choose where to refer the patient, give the reason, answer the request form,

1.3
00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.035
check the referral, and send it.

2.1
00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:17.947
Step 2. In Destination, open Refer to and select Departments.

2.2
00:00:17.947 --> 00:00:22.685
You can refer to a facility, a department, or an organization.

2.3
00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:25.477
Refer to starts at Facilities.

3.1
00:00:25.477 --> 00:00:29.788
Step 3. Open Referral unit and select the referral availability.

3.2
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:34.794
Care shows it under Destination and fills Referral title with its name.

4.1
00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:40.035
Step 4. Under Reason for referral, check Referral title, which is required.

4.2
00:00:40.035 --> 00:00:45.327
Then enter context for the receiving team in Additional note (optional).

5.1
00:00:45.327 --> 00:00:50.410
Step 5. Under Service questions, answer the questions of the request form.

5.2
00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.089
A red asterisk marks a required question.

5.3
00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:58.053
Your answers go with the referral and do not create clinical records for the

5.4
00:00:58.053 --> 00:00:59.179
patient.

6.1
00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:02.674
Step 6. Select Review referral at the top right.

6.2
00:01:02.674 --> 00:01:08.786
Nothing has been sent yet, so check the referral unit, the reason, and the answers.

7.1
00:01:08.786 --> 00:01:12.389
Step 7. Select Send referral at the top right.

7.2
00:01:12.389 --> 00:01:15.669
Care closes the form and shows Referral sent.

7.3
00:01:15.669 --> 00:01:19.085
The new referral has the status Pending.
